    ; stored as any assignment is, while a live action of its own is open, whose trackers note what
    ; the value reads. Then the action is made with those trackers and a callback that runs the
    ; statement again through the function written for it, given the environment in force here,
    ; and the object named alone whose property is assigned, read again, owns the action where it
    ; is of a class. Where that class is a markup host or batch, the action is made as the type
    ; pass chose for it (`LiveStatement`), given the object as its host or its batch.
